{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Many</b> — from the king's officers. That is, <b>and a noble</b> [נדיב] — because his heart volunteers to give to the poor, his stature grows, until the great ones entreat his face to help them or to love them, as in 'they entreat your face with a gift' [תגדל מעלתו... מנחה פניך יחלו], and all the friends join to a man of giving [איש מתן] — to a man who gives them gifts." "And the word <b>they distance themselves</b> [רחקו] — plural form compounded from singulars." "<b>from his friend</b> [מרעהו] — it is one. Its meaning: each and every one, until they all distance themselves." "<b>And pursues</b> [ומרדף] — verb transitive to the true object acted upon, for the poor man is the pursuer." "<b>And those sent</b> [והאמרים] — they are the pursuers, and the brothers or the friends are the pursued, as in 'his enemies—darkness pursues' [ואויביו ירדף חשך] and 'she pursues her lovers' [ורדפה את מאהביה]. And the matter connects above with 'and a poor man is separated from his friend' [ודל מרעהו יפרד]: all the brothers of the poor and destitute hate him; all the more so his friends, who distanced themselves from him after their joining to him, because of his gifts. And the poor man commands to pursue after them, sending [לוחי?] his sayings, perhaps his friends will draw near to him — but they do not listen."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {4 "Reading לוחי as possibly corrupt; translated hyper-literally. The word is unclear—could be a corruption of שולחי ('those sending')."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:23:42.649242764Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}